"Game: Galaxigans — Galaxian-style fixed shooter, ported from x64 assembler"
"galaxigans.mst — GALAXIGANS: a Galaxian/Galaga-style fixed shooter for the
 native Metal game pane, ported from the x64 assembler original in
 MRASM/projects/galaxigans (6251 lines of .was across 35 files).

 THIS FILE IS THE GAME. It lives in demos/ with the other playable files, not
 in the built-in world: picking it from the Games menu files its classes into
 the running image and starts it, and the Edit button opens THIS FILE — all
 five classes — where Save writes back to disk. A game in st/world/ would be
 part of the system image instead: editable only one class at a time through
 the Browser, and overwritten by the next world import.

 The port is deliberately FAITHFUL to that game's numbers rather than a vague
 homage — every constant below comes from its galaxigans_data.inc, so the two
 can be compared side by side: a 640x360 field, an 8x5 formation of 16x16
 aliens on a 56x34 grid from (96,56), sway +/-16 at 1px a frame, a dive every 60
 frames that peels for 12 then homes, divers returning down the screen at 4px a
 frame to re-dock in their own slot, 4 bullets at 7px a frame on an 8-frame
 cooldown, 6 bombs at 4px a frame every 22, a bonus saucer every 420 frames
 worth 200, and a 90-frame respawn beat.

 The dive AI is the heart of Galaga and the most interesting thing to port. It
 is the original's, transcribed: each dive gets a random seed whose bits ARE the
 flight plan — weave speed ((seed>>3)&7)+3, weave phase (seed>>8)&255, weave
 amplitude (seed&7)+2, plus a 'fast' bit raising the descent cap from 8 to 10
 and a 'hard' bit tripling the homing pull. So no two swoops trace the same
 curve, and the fleet's behaviour is emergent rather than scripted.

 Ported since: the ten-species creature library and the twelve-level table with
 the original's own cosmos shaders (layer 0), the saucer's beating wah-wah, its
 rare SPINNING MINE (threat and treat — it kills the ship, and it pays 150 to
 shoot), and the triumphal VICTORY DANCE the survivors perform over the
 game-over card.

 And now the CAPTURE BOSS with its tractor beam, and the pilot row it comes
 for: the boss enters, stations, descends to the middle of the field, charges,
 and fires a beam down into your pilots. One rises up it; if it reaches the
 boss that life is gone, and if you shoot the boss first the pilot drops home
 saved and you take 500. It will not appear at all when you are down to a last
 pilot — the original's own rule, and the right one.

 The beam is drawn ONCE per frame as a cone in palette index 1, and flows by
 rewriting what index 1 MEANS on each scanline — the pane's per-line palette,
 which is the copper-bar mechanism and the original's own (BeamCascade). No
 pixel is redrawn to animate it.

 And the music: the original's four melodic cues (galaxigans_music.was) are
 transcribed note for note — the choir build on the title screen, the
 glockenspiel fanfare for a cleared wave, the pad swell that announces the
 saucer, and 'Alien Victory', the square-lead triumph the aliens dance to when
 they have taken your last ship. Its percussion cues are not ported: the pane's
 SFX presets already play that part, and doubling them would only muddy it.

 And the HIGH-SCORE TABLE — with the port's best trick: the hall of fame is a
 CLASS IN THE IMAGE (GxHallOfFame), created and rewritten by the game itself
 through the browser's own checked accept, so your scores are source, they are
 browsable, and they survive a full restart because the image is the source of
 truth. It is deliberately not part of this file: re-filing the game in can
 never clobber it.

 What is still NOT ported: the original's nano-TCL dev channel — this
 workspace's own control plane already does that job.

 Controls: Left/Right steer, Space fires (tap, no autofire — the original's
 shoot_held/shoot_release beat). Launch from the GAMES menu, or a Workspace:
     Galaxigans launch

 This runs on a 640x360 pane, wider than the 320x240 the other Smalltalk games
 open (macdart/cocoa/workspace/language.dart, _kStGames 'size'), so there is
 room for a real fleet and a HUD in the pane's own 5x7 font."

"--- one alien: a slot in the formation, and its own flight plan while diving ---"
"I am one Galaxigan. In formation I track my home slot plus the fleet's sway;
 when launched I fly my own swooping dive at the player, drop out of the bottom
 of the field, and glide back down from the top into my slot to dive again. My
 dive is not scripted: the random seed I am launched with packs the weave speed,
 phase and amplitude, and two behaviour bits, so every swoop is different."
"Forward-declare this file's own classes before the definitions below. MACVM
 installs classes top-to-bottom and a bare READ of a class global that is not
 yet installed is a compile error (unlike a genesis class such as Association,
 which is pre-registered) — and these classes reference each other mutually
 (Galaxigan names Galaxigans for its dive maths; Galaxigans names all the
 rest). A top-level assignment auto-declares the uppercase global; each
 `subclass:` below then binds it to the real class. (GamePane/Sprite/Sound/
 Tune/Random are already global from 43_gamepane.mst.)"
Object subclass: Galaxigan [ | x y homeX homeY state kind dt seed bank alive sprite species | ]
Object subclass: GxShot [ | x y dy live | ]
Object subclass: GxMine [ | x y anim live sprite | ]
Object subclass: GxBoss [ | state x y anim timer beamT sprite | ]
Object subclass: GxSpark [ | x y vx vy life colour | ]
Object subclass: GxSpecies [ | name art art2 palette | ]
Object subclass: Galaxigans [
    <classVars: Sine Species Current Hall>
    | pane rng gameState stateTimer frame
      shipX shipSprite lives score hiScore wave respawn
      fleet swayX swayDir diveTimer bombTimer
      bullets bombs mines sparks level scene theme flap danceT
      mineDrops saucerDrops hiTable hiNewRow
      boss bossOn pilots abducting abducteeX abducteeY beamPhase pilotsTaken
      saucer saucerX saucerDir saucerTimer saucerWah saucerBombT
      cooldown fireWasDown |
]

Object subclass: Galaxigan [

    Galaxigan class >> homeX: hx homeY: hy kind: aKind [
        ^self new setHomeX: hx homeY: hy kind: aKind
    ]

    setHomeX: hx homeY: hy kind: aKind [
        homeX := hx. homeY := hy. kind := aKind.
        x := hx. y := hy.
        state := #form. dt := 0. seed := 0. bank := 0. alive := true.
        ^self
    ]

    x [ ^x ]
    y [ ^y ]
    homeX [ ^homeX ]
    homeY [ ^homeY ]
    kind [ ^kind ]
    species [ ^species ]

    "My species is an index into the game's creature library; my two flap
     frames sit at (index-1)*2 and +1 on my sprite's definition, which carries
     every species' art (see Galaxigans>>buildSprites)."
    species: anIndex name: aName [ species := anIndex. kind := aName ]
    frameFor: flap [ ^(species isNil ifTrue: [ 1 ] ifFalse: [ species ]) - 1 * 2 + flap ]
    state [ ^state ]
    alive [ ^alive ]
    isDiving [ ^state == #dive ]
    sprite [ ^sprite ]
    sprite: s [ sprite := s ]

    kill [ alive := false. state := #dead ]

    "Score is by row: the front rank is worth least, and a diver is worth
     double — the arcade's own bargain, take the risk for the points."
    points [
        "The rarer species (higher up the library) are worth more, and a diver
         is worth double — the arcade's own bargain, take the risk for points."
        | base |
        base := 40 + ((species isNil ifTrue: [ 1 ] ifFalse: [ species ]) * 10).
        ^state == #dive ifTrue: [ base * 2 ] ifFalse: [ base ]
    ]

    "Launch me at the player. The seed IS the flight plan (see the class
     comment); dt drives both the descent ramp and the weave."
    diveWithSeed: s [
        state := #dive. dt := 0. seed := s
    ]

    "One frame of formation flight: sit in my slot, carried by the sway."
    followFormation: swayX [
        x := homeX + swayX. y := homeY. bank := 0
    ]

    "One frame of the glide home: drop from above the field into my own slot,
     tracking the swaying column on the way in."
    returnStep: swayX [
        y := y + 4.
        x := homeX + swayX.
        bank := 0.
        y >= homeY ifTrue: [ y := homeY. state := #form ]
    ]

    "One frame of the dive — the ported swoop. Answers true when I have left
     the bottom of the field and should re-enter from the top."
    diveStep: playerX height: fieldH [
        | vy weave amp speed phase pull |
        dt := dt + 1.
        vy := 2 + (dt // 4).
        vy := vy min: ((seed bitAnd: 128) = 0 ifTrue: [ 8 ] ifFalse: [ 10 ]).
        y := y + vy.
        speed := ((seed bitShift: -3) bitAnd: 7) + 3.
        phase := ((seed bitShift: -8) bitAnd: 255).
        amp := (seed bitAnd: 7) + 2.
        weave := (Galaxigans sineAt: dt * speed + phase) * amp // 256.
        "The peel: for the first 12 steps I only weave, so I break formation
         outward before I start hunting. After that the homing pull leans me
         toward the player — gently, or hard if my seed says so."
        dt >= 12 ifTrue: [
            pull := (seed bitAnd: 64) = 0 ifTrue: [ 1 ] ifFalse: [ 3 ].
            weave := x < playerX
                ifTrue: [ weave + pull ]
                ifFalse: [ weave - pull ] ].
        x := x + weave.
        bank := weave sign.
        y > (fieldH + 8) ifTrue: [ ^true ].
        ^false
    ]

    "Put me exactly here — the victory dance flies the fleet itself."
    moveToX: ax y: ay [ x := ax. y := ay. bank := 0 ]

    "Re-enter from above, ready to glide back into my slot."
    reenterAt: swayX [
        state := #return. dt := 0. x := homeX + swayX. y := -20
    ]

    "My hit box, generous by half a pixel in the player's favour."
    hits: px y: py halfWidth: hw [
        ^alive and: [ (x - px) abs < (hw + 8) and: [ (y - py) abs < 12 ] ]
    ]
]

"--- a shot: one player bullet, or one enemy bomb ---"
"I am one projectile in a fixed-size pool — a player bullet flying up, or an
 enemy bomb falling. The pool never grows during play: the original DIMs four
 bullets and six bombs, and running out IS the game's rate limit."
Object subclass: GxShot [

    "`super new` is not compilable here (the ST engine's flow-graph builder
     refuses self/super in a class-method receiver position), so the pool asks
     for `empty` rather than overriding new."
    GxShot class >> empty [ ^self new setDead ]
    setDead [ live := false. x := 0. y := 0. dy := 0. ^self ]

    x [ ^x ]
    y [ ^y ]
    live [ ^live ]
    kill [ live := false ]

    fireFrom: ax y: ay dy: ady [
        x := ax. y := ay. dy := ady. live := true
    ]

    "Advance one frame; answers false when I leave the field."
    stepIn: fieldH [
        live ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        y := y + dy.
        (y < -8 or: [ y > (fieldH + 8) ]) ifTrue: [ live := false. ^false ].
        ^true
    ]

    hits: tx y: ty halfWidth: hw halfHeight: hh [
        ^live and: [ (x - tx) abs < hw and: [ (y - ty) abs < hh ] ]
    ]
]


"--- the saucer's rare spinning mine ---"
"I am a space mine: the bonus saucer drops me instead of a bomb about one time
 in eight. I drift down slowly, spinning, and I am both threat and treat —
 touching the ship kills it, shooting me pays 150. The original files me under
 'the rare spinning mine the saucer sometimes drops' and gives me eight
 rotation frames; I turn one full circle every 32 frames."
Object subclass: GxMine [

    GxMine class >> empty [ ^self new setDead ]
    setDead [ live := false. x := 0. y := 0. anim := 0. ^self ]

    x [ ^x ]
    y [ ^y ]
    live [ ^live ]
    kill [ live := false ]
    sprite [ ^sprite ]
    sprite: s [ sprite := s ]
    "Eight frames, advancing every fourth tick."
    frame [ ^(anim // 4) \\ 8 ]

    dropAt: ax y: ay [ x := ax. y := ay. anim := 0. live := true ]

    "Half a pixel a frame: it drifts DOWN on the odd ticks only, so it hangs in
     the field far longer than a bomb and has to be dealt with."
    stepIn: fieldH [
        live ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        anim := anim + 1.
        (anim bitAnd: 1) = 1 ifTrue: [ y := y + 1 ].
        y > (fieldH + 8) ifTrue: [ live := false. ^false ].
        ^true
    ]

    hits: tx y: ty halfWidth: hw halfHeight: hh [
        ^live and: [ (x - tx) abs < (hw + 8) and: [ (y - ty) abs < (hh + 8) ] ]
    ]
]

"--- the capture boss ---"
"I am the capture boss: a 32x32 crab that comes for your PILOTS, not your ship.
 I enter from the top, hover, then descend to the middle of the field, charge,
 and fire a tractor beam down into the row of pilots along the bottom. A pilot
 rises up the beam; if it reaches me you lose that life. Shoot me while I am
 down there and the pilot drops home, saved, and I am worth 500.

 The lifecycle is the original's (galaxigans_boss.was): idle, enter, station,
 descend, charge, beam, return — with its own rule that I never appear, and
 never grab, when the player is down to a LAST pilot. Bullying someone out of
 their final life is not a mechanic, it is just cruelty."
Object subclass: GxBoss [

    GxBoss class >> empty [ ^self new setIdle ]
    setIdle [
        state := #idle. x := 304. y := -36. anim := 0. beamT := 0.
        timer := Galaxigans bossFirst.
        ^self
    ]

    state [ ^state ]
    x [ ^x ]
    y [ ^y ]
    beamT [ ^beamT ]
    sprite [ ^sprite ]
    sprite: s [ sprite := s ]
    isIdle [ ^state == #idle ]
    "Down where a bullet can reach me — descending, charging or firing."
    isVulnerable [
        ^state == #descend or: [ state == #charge or: [ state == #beam ] ]
    ]
    isBeaming [ ^state == #charge or: [ state == #beam ] ]

    "Which of my four frames: two idle poses alternating, then the charge and
     beam poses — the emitter eye grows, which is the tell."
    frame [
        state == #beam ifTrue: [ ^3 ].
        state == #charge ifTrue: [ ^2 ].
        ^(anim // 16) \\ 2
    ]

    "The beam's mouth, and how far down it has grown."
    beamX [ ^x + 16 ]
    beamTop [ ^y + 24 ]
    beamBottom: fieldH [
        state == #beam ifTrue: [ ^350 ].
        ^(y + 24 + (beamT * 14)) min: 350
    ]

    wake [ state := #enter. x := 304. y := -36. anim := 0 ]
    retreat [ state := #return ]
    vanish [ state := #idle. y := -60. timer := Galaxigans bossRespawn ]

    "One frame. Answers a symbol the game acts on: #none, #charged (start the
     hum), #grab (a pilot is in the beam) or #done."
    stepWithLives: lives enabled: enabled [
        anim := anim + 1.
        state == #idle ifTrue: [
            (enabled and: [ lives > 1 ]) ifFalse: [ ^#none ].
            timer := timer - 1.
            timer > 0 ifTrue: [ ^#none ].
            self wake.
            ^#warn ].
        state == #enter ifTrue: [
            y < Galaxigans bossStationY
                ifTrue: [ y := y + 2 ]
                ifFalse: [ state := #station. timer := Galaxigans bossDwell ].
            ^#none ].
        state == #station ifTrue: [
            timer := timer - 1.
            timer > 0 ifTrue: [ ^#none ].
            "Down to the last pilot? Give up and go home."
            lives <= 1 ifTrue: [ state := #return. ^#none ].
            state := #descend.
            ^#none ].
        state == #descend ifTrue: [
            x := x < 304 ifTrue: [ x + 3 ] ifFalse: [ x - 3 ].
            y < Galaxigans bossCaptureY
                ifTrue: [ y := y + 3. ^#none ].
            state := #charge. beamT := 0.
            ^#charged ].
        state == #charge ifTrue: [
            beamT := beamT + 1.
            beamT < Galaxigans beamCharge ifTrue: [ ^#none ].
            state := #beam. beamT := 0.
            ^#charged ].
        state == #beam ifTrue: [
            beamT := beamT + 1.
            beamT >= Galaxigans beamHold ifTrue: [ state := #return. ^#done ].
            ^#grab ].
        state == #return ifTrue: [
            y := y - 4.
            y < -40 ifTrue: [ self vanish ].
            ^#none ].
        ^#none
    ]

    "A bullet in my 32x32 box, while I am down."
    hits: bx y: by [
        ^self isVulnerable and: [
            bx >= x and: [ bx < (x + 32) and: [ by >= y and: [ by < (y + 32) ] ] ] ]
    ]
]

"--- explosion debris ---"
"I am one spark of an explosion: a coloured pixel with a velocity and a life.
 A burst of me is the whole particle system — the original ran the same idea
 through its PtBurst/PtUpdate pool."
Object subclass: GxSpark [

    GxSpark class >> at: ax y: ay vx: avx vy: avy colour: c [
        ^self new setX: ax y: ay vx: avx vy: avy colour: c
    ]
    setX: ax y: ay vx: avx vy: avy colour: c [
        x := ax. y := ay. vx := avx. vy := avy. colour := c. life := 18. ^self
    ]

    x [ ^x ]
    y [ ^y ]
    colour [ ^colour ]
    live [ ^life > 0 ]

    step [
        x := x + vx. y := y + vy. vy := vy + 1. life := life - 1
    ]
]

"--- one alien species: its art, its animation, its palette ---"
"I am one species of Galaxigan — two frames of 16x16 art and the ten-colour
 palette they index. Both come VERBATIM from the assembler original's creature
 library (galaxigans_aliens2.was): its rows are '.'-plus-hex exactly like the
 pane's own defineSprite: format, and its palette is the comment block above
 each table. Ten of us exist; a level's formation theme picks five, one per
 row of the grid."
Object subclass: GxSpecies [

    GxSpecies class >> name: n art: a art2: b palette: p [
        ^self new setName: n art: a art2: b palette: p
    ]
    setName: n art: a art2: b palette: p [
        name := n. art := a. art2 := b. palette := p. ^self
    ]

    name [ ^name ]
    art [ ^art ]
    art2 [ ^art2 ]

    "Paint my ten colours onto a sprite. The palette array is flat — r,g,b per
     index, index 1 first (0 is the sprite format's transparent)."
    paint: aSprite [
        1 to: 10 do: [ :i |
            aSprite
                colorAt: i
                r: (palette at: (i - 1) * 3 + 1)
                g: (palette at: (i - 1) * 3 + 2)
                b: (palette at: (i - 1) * 3 + 3) ].
        ^self
    ]
]

"--- the game ---"
"I am GALAXIGANS, a Galaxian/Galaga-style fixed shooter on the native game
 pane, ported from an x64 assembler original (see the file comment). Left and
 Right steer, Space fires — one shot per press, four in flight. Shoot the
 formation before it dives you out of lives; the bonus saucer overhead is worth
 200. Launch me from the GAMES menu or a Workspace: Galaxigans launch."
Object subclass: Galaxigans [
    "classVars + ivars are declared in the forward shell above (MACVM rejects a
     reopen that re-declares shape); this reopen adds only methods."

    "--- the field, straight from the original's galaxigans_data.inc ---"
    Galaxigans class >> fieldWidth [ ^640 ]
    Galaxigans class >> fieldHeight [ ^360 ]
    "The pane I want when I am filed in from demos/ — the driver asks a game
     for these rather than keeping its resolution in a table elsewhere."
    Galaxigans class >> paneWidth [ ^self fieldWidth ]
    Galaxigans class >> paneHeight [ ^self fieldHeight ]
    Galaxigans class >> playerY [ ^310 ]
    Galaxigans class >> cols [ ^8 ]
    Galaxigans class >> rows [ ^5 ]
    Galaxigans class >> colGap [ ^56 ]
    Galaxigans class >> rowGap [ ^34 ]
    Galaxigans class >> gridX [ ^96 ]
    Galaxigans class >> gridY [ ^56 ]
    Galaxigans class >> divePeriod [ ^60 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bombPeriod [ ^22 ]
    Galaxigans class >> saucerPeriod [ ^420 ]
    "The triumphal dance (galaxigans_dance.was): the survivors orbit the middle
     of the field on a breathing-radius pinwheel while the game-over card sits
     over them. Centre is the field's, the radius breathes R0 +/- R1, and each
     alien is offset around the wheel by its index."
    Galaxigans class >> danceCX [ ^320 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceCY [ ^180 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceR0 [ ^95 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceR1 [ ^70 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceAngleStep [ ^6 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceRadStep [ ^10 ]
    Galaxigans class >> danceLength [ ^420 ]
    "The attract cycle, in frames at the ~33fps pull rate: the title holds for
     ~18s, the hall of fame for ~30s, and then round again — the machine never
     stops on its own, it just waits for a player."
    Galaxigans class >> attractLength [ ^600 ]
    Galaxigans class >> hiscoreLength [ ^1000 ]

    "--- the hall of fame: a CLASS IN THE IMAGE, written by the game ---------"
    "The original keeps six rows in .DATA — ACE 30000 down to WOW 4000 — and
     slots your score in as YOU. Here the table is a real class,
     GxHallOfFame, that the game CREATES AND REWRITES through the browser's
     own checked accept (STHostService acceptEditorClass:): parse-checked,
     persisted in the SQLite image, hot-reloaded live. Your scores survive a
     restart because they live in the image — and the hall is BROWSABLE: open
     GxHallOfFame in the Browser and there they are, as source. It is a
     separate class, not part of this file, precisely so that re-filing the
     game in from the Games menu can never clobber it."
    Galaxigans class >> defaultHall [
        ^#( #('ACE' 30000) #('ZAP' 22000) #('BUG' 16000)
            #('FOE' 11000) #('POW' 7000)  #('WOW' 4000) )
    ]

    "The persisted hall if the image holds one, else the defaults. Resolved by
     REFLECTION rather than a bare global: naming an undefined class in source
     would be a compile error, and headless (no image host) the class simply
     never exists."
    Galaxigans class >> loadHall [
        "MACVM adaptation: MACDART persisted the hall as a GxHallOfFame class
         re-accepted through the Cocoa Browser's host service (STHostService),
         which this VM's primary game process has no reach to. Here the hall
         lives in the `Hall` class variable — it persists across games WITHIN a
         launch (attract -> play -> hall -> newGame all see the same table), and
         resets to the defaults on a fresh launch. Cross-launch persistence via
         the SQLite image is a follow-up (docs/gamepane_design.md)."
        Hall isNil ifTrue: [ ^self defaultHall asOrderedCollection ].
        ^Hall asOrderedCollection
    ]

    "GxHallOfFame's whole source, holding [rows] as a literal table."
    Galaxigans class >> hallSourceFor: rows [
        | w |
        w := WriteStream on: String new.
        w nextPutAll: '"GxHallOfFame - the Galaxigans high-score table. WRITTEN BY THE GAME:'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: ' each new score re-accepts this class through the same checked path the'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: ' Browser uses, so the table persists in the image and survives restarts.'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: ' Edit it here if you like - it is only source."'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: 'Object subclass: GxHallOfFame ['; nl.
        w nextPutAll: '    GxHallOfFame class >> table ['; nl.
        w nextPutAll: '        ^#('.
        rows do: [ :r |
            w nextPutAll: ' #('''.
            w nextPutAll: (r at: 1).
            w nextPutAll: ''' '.
            w nextPutAll: (r at: 2) printString.
            w nextPutAll: ')' ].
        w nextPutAll: ' )'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: '    ]'; nl.
        w nextPutAll: ']'; nl.
        ^w contents
    ]

    "Persist [rows] as GxHallOfFame. In the GUI this goes through the image
     host and answers 'OK ...'; headless there is no host and the reply is an
     ERR string — the game keeps its in-memory table and shrugs, which is why
     the battery can drive the whole flow without a window.

     STORE, not accept: we are saving from inside the frame callback. The
     Browser's acceptEditorClass: hot-reloads the WHOLE world, which re-inits
     every class's class-side state — including GamePane's StepBlock, the
     per-frame closure that IS the frame loop. That froze the game on the very
     frame it saved (the hall of fame came up and never timed out), and the
     game could not rescue itself: this method's globals are already bound to
     the pre-reload class, while the driver resolves GamePane by name and gets
     the new one. storeEditorClass: parse-checks and persists identically, but
     makes only GxHallOfFame live, so the loop underneath keeps running."
    Galaxigans class >> saveHall: rows [
        "MACVM adaptation (see loadHall): store the table in the `Hall` class
         variable rather than re-accepting a GxHallOfFame class through the
         Browser host service. Safe to call from inside the frame callback (no
         world reload, so GamePane's StepBlock — the frame loop itself — is
         untouched, which is exactly the freeze MACDART's storeEditorClass:
         note was avoiding). Answers a status string like the original."
        Hall := rows asOrderedCollection.
        ^'hall saved (', Hall size printString, ' rows, in-memory)'
    ]

    "The capture boss (galaxigans_data.inc), and the pilot row it comes for."
    Galaxigans class >> bossFirst [ ^40 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bossDwell [ ^60 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bossRespawn [ ^360 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bossStationY [ ^18 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bossCaptureY [ ^140 ]
    Galaxigans class >> bossScore [ ^500 ]
    Galaxigans class >> beamCharge [ ^30 ]
    Galaxigans class >> beamHold [ ^90 ]
    Galaxigans class >> pilotRowY [ ^344 ]
    Galaxigans class >> pilotX0 [ ^14 ]
    Galaxigans class >> pilotGap [ ^16 ]
    "The original flies its saucer at y=20; here the HUD's own row is up there
     (5x7 at scale 2 = fourteen pixels from y=8), so it crosses just below,
     clear of the score."
    Galaxigans class >> saucerY [ ^30 ]
    Galaxigans class >> saucerBombGap [ ^28 ]
    Galaxigans class >> mineScore [ ^150 ]

    Galaxigans class >> launch [
        "Open the pane and start a new game."
        ^self new start
    ]

    "The game that is running, if any — so a script (or the Workspace) can
     reach it: `Galaxigans current forceNextWave`, `Galaxigans current summary`."
    Galaxigans class >> current [ ^Current ]
    Galaxigans class >> register: aGame [ Current := aGame ]

    "A 256-entry sine table in [-256,256], built once. The original carried a
     sineLUT in .DATA for exactly this reason: the dive weave asks for a sine
     per diver per frame, and a table keeps the whole flight path in integers —
     no float in the inner loop, and the same curve every run."
    Galaxigans class >> sineAt: i [
        Sine isNil ifTrue: [ self buildSine ].
        ^Sine at: (i \\ 256) + 1
    ]
    Galaxigans class >> buildSine [
        | t |
        t := Array new: 256.
        1 to: 256 do: [ :k |
            t at: k put: (((k - 1) * 6.283185307179586 / 256.0) sin * 256.0) rounded ].
        Sine := t
    ]

    start [
        Current := self.
        hiTable := Galaxigans loadHall.
        hiNewRow := 0.
        pane := GamePane new.
        "MACVM's game pane defaults to 320x240; galaxigans is a 640x360 field.
         Request the size FIRST, before any draw, so the pane is created at it
         (43_gamepane.mst GamePane>>resizeTo:by:)."
        pane resizeTo: 640 by: 360.
        "My motion and timers were tuned for the original's ~33fps pull rate.
         MACVM's game pane runs at 60fps by default, which plays me twice too
         fast and piles up sound triggers, so ask for 30 (GamePane>>frameRate:)."
        pane frameRate: 30.
        rng := Random new.
        frame := 0.
        hiScore := 0.
        self buildPalette.
        pane shader: self class cosmosShader.   "layer 0: the twelve cosmos"
        self buildSprites.
        self newGame.
        pane onStep: [ self step ]; run.
        ^self
    ]

    "--- setup ------------------------------------------------------------"

    buildPalette [
        "The indexed layer is drawn OVER the shader, so it is cleared to index
         0 (transparent) every frame and carries only what the game plots:
         20 bullet, 21 bomb, 22/23 spark. The background is the shader's now —
         which is also where the original's stars live."
        pane paletteAt: 20 r: 255 g: 240 b: 120.
        pane paletteAt: 21 r: 255 g: 90  b: 220.
        pane paletteAt: 22 r: 255 g: 200 b: 60.
        pane paletteAt: 23 r: 255 g: 80  b: 40.
    ]

    buildSprites [
        "One sprite instance per formation slot, built ONCE — and each of them
         carries EVERY species' art as frames: ten species x two flap frames,
         all 16x16, so a level change is a frame offset and a repaint, not a
         new sprite. (The pane's Smalltalk face defines and places in one call,
         and the engine numbers defs per pane-open, so re-defining forty
         sprites a level would pile up definitions for no reason.)"
        shipSprite := pane defineSprite: self class shipArt.
        shipSprite colorAt: 1 r: 230 g: 240 b: 255.
        shipSprite colorAt: 2 r: 255 g: 140 b: 40.
        shipSprite colorAt: 3 r: 60  g: 140 b: 255.
        shipSprite colorAt: 4 r: 255 g: 70  b: 70.

        saucer := pane defineSprite: self class saucerArt.
        saucer colorAt: 1 r: 220 g: 220 b: 230.
        saucer colorAt: 2 r: 120 g: 120 b: 140.
        saucer colorAt: 3 r: 90  g: 220 b: 255.
        saucer colorAt: 4 r: 255 g: 220 b: 90.
        saucer hide.

        "The capture boss: one sprite, four frames."
        boss := GxBoss empty.
        boss sprite: (pane defineSprite: (self class bossArt at: 1)).
        2 to: 4 do: [ :k | boss sprite addFrame: (self class bossArt at: k) ].
        self paintSprite: boss sprite with: self class bossPalette count: 12.
        boss sprite hide.

        "The pilots: one sprite per life, standing in a row along the bottom.
         These are what the boss's beam comes for."
        pilots := (1 to: 4) collect: [ :i | | spr |
            spr := pane defineSprite: self class pilotArt.
            self paintSprite: spr with: self class pilotPalette count: 7.
            spr hide.
            spr ].

        "Six mines, each a sprite carrying all eight spin frames."
        mines := (1 to: 6) collect: [ :i | GxMine empty ].
        mines do: [ :m | | spr pal |
            spr := pane defineSprite: (self class mineArt at: 1).
            2 to: 8 do: [ :k | spr addFrame: (self class mineArt at: k) ].
            pal := self class minePalette.
            1 to: 8 do: [ :k |
                spr colorAt: k
                    r: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 1)
                    g: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 2)
                    b: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 3) ].
            spr hide.
            m sprite: spr ].

        fleet := OrderedCollection new.
        1 to: self class rows do: [ :r |
            1 to: self class cols do: [ :c | | alien spr |
                alien := Galaxigan
                    homeX: self class gridX + ((c - 1) * self class colGap)
                    homeY: self class gridY + ((r - 1) * self class rowGap)
                    kind: #grunt.
                spr := pane defineSprite: (self class species at: 1) art.
                spr addFrame: (self class species at: 1) art2.
                2 to: self class species size do: [ :k |
                    spr addFrame: (self class species at: k) art.
                    spr addFrame: (self class species at: k) art2 ].
                spr hide.
                alien sprite: spr.
                fleet add: alien ] ]
    ]

    paintSprite: aSprite with: pal count: n [
        1 to: n do: [ :k |
            aSprite colorAt: k
                r: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 1)
                g: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 2)
                b: (pal at: (k - 1) * 3 + 3) ]
    ]

    "Dress the fleet for this level: each row becomes one species — its art is
     already loaded as frames, so this is a frame offset plus its palette."
    dressFleet [
        | rowSpecies |
        rowSpecies := self class themes at: theme.
        1 to: fleet size do: [ :i | | a row sp |
            a := fleet at: i.
            row := (i - 1) // self class cols + 1.
            sp := self class species at: (rowSpecies at: row).
            a species: (rowSpecies at: row) name: sp name.
            sp paint: a sprite ]
    ]

    newGame [
        score := 0.
        lives := 3.
        wave := 1.
        flap := 0.
        gameState := #attract.
        stateTimer := self class attractLength.
        self startWave
    ]

    startWave [
        "Rebuild the fleet's state (the objects persist; a wave is a reset, not
         a reallocation), pick this level's cosmos and formation, and re-arm the
         timers. The level table wraps, so wave 13 is level 1's backdrop again —
         with wave 13's dive cadence."
        level := (wave - 1) \\ self class levels size + 1.
        scene := (self class levels at: level) at: 1.
        theme := (self class levels at: level) at: 2.
        pane shaderParam: 0 value: scene.
        shipX := self class fieldWidth // 2.
        respawn := 0.
        cooldown := 0.
        fireWasDown := false.
        swayX := 0. swayDir := 1.
        diveTimer := self divePeriodNow.
        bombTimer := self class bombPeriod.
        saucerX := -60. saucerDir := 0. saucerTimer := self class saucerPeriod.
        saucerWah := 0.
        saucerBombT := self class saucerBombGap.
        fleet do: [ :a | a setHomeX: a homeX homeY: a homeY kind: a kind ].
        self dressFleet.
        bullets := (1 to: 4) collect: [ :i | GxShot empty ].
        bombs := (1 to: 6) collect: [ :i | GxShot empty ].
        mines do: [ :m | m kill ].
        mineDrops := 0. saucerDrops := 0.
        bossOn := ((self class levels at: level) at: 3) = 1.
        boss setIdle.
        abducting := 0. abducteeX := 0. abducteeY := 0. beamPhase := 0.
        pilotsTaken isNil ifTrue: [ pilotsTaken := 0 ].
        sparks := OrderedCollection new
    ]

    "Each wave dives harder — the original ramps gDivePeriod the same way."
    divePeriodNow [ ^(self class divePeriod - (wave - 1 * 6)) max: 18 ]

    "State, readable — for a headless test or a scripted probe. The game runs
     perfectly well with no window (every pane primitive is a no-op there), so
     the whole of it can be driven and asserted on from the battery."
    gameState [ ^gameState ]
    score [ ^score ]
    lives [ ^lives ]
    wave [ ^wave ]
    aliveCount [
        | n |
        n := 0.
        fleet do: [ :a | a alive ifTrue: [ n := n + 1 ] ].
        ^n
    ]

    "Which cosmos and which creatures this level fields — the level table,
     read back. Used by the battery to walk all twelve."
    levelReport [
        | names |
        names := OrderedCollection new.
        (self class themes at: theme) do: [ :k |
            names add: (self class species at: k) name printString ].
        ^'L', level printString, ' ', (self class sceneNames at: scene + 1),
         ' [', (names inject: '' into: [ :a :b | a isEmpty ifTrue: [ b ] ifFalse: [ a, ' ', b ] ]), ']'
    ]

    "Send the bonus saucer across now, instead of waiting out its 420-frame
     timer — for a test, or for anyone who wants to hear the warble."
    summonSaucer [ saucerTimer := 1 ]

    "Set the score — so a test (or a workspace doit) can walk a chosen score
     into the hall without earning it."
    setScore: n [ score := n ]

    "The hall as one line per row — for the battery and the control plane."
    hallReport [
        | w |
        w := WriteStream on: String new.
        1 to: hiTable size do: [ :i | | r |
            r := hiTable at: i.
            w nextPutAll: i printString, ' ', (r at: 1), ' ', (r at: 2) printString.
            w nl ].
        w nextPutAll: 'new row ', hiNewRow printString.
        ^w contents
    ]

    "Set the lives, so a test can put the player on their last pilot — the one
     state the boss is supposed to leave alone."
    setLives: n [ lives := n ]

    "Start the victory dance now, without dying three times for it."
    danceNow [ self beginDance ]

    "The aliens have won: they leave formation, and their own tune plays over
     it — the square-lead 'Alien Victory' from the original's music file."
    beginDance [
        gameState := #over.
        stateTimer := self class danceLength.
        danceT := 0.
        (Tune fromAbc: self class tuneAlienVictory) playOnce
    ]

    "How many mines are in the field, and where the fleet is relative to its
     formation — the two new features, readable for the battery."
    mineReport [
        | n |
        n := 0.
        mines do: [ :m | m live ifTrue: [ n := n + 1 ] ].
        ^'mines ', n printString, ' (dropped ', mineDrops printString,
         ' of ', saucerDrops printString, ' saucer drops)'
    ]

    "How far the fleet has left its slots: 0 in formation, large mid-dance."
    danceSpread [
        | d n |
        d := 0. n := 0.
        fleet do: [ :a |
            a alive ifTrue: [
                d := d + (a y - a homeY) abs. n := n + 1 ] ].
        ^n = 0 ifTrue: [ 0 ] ifFalse: [ d // n ]
    ]

    "The boss's state and what the beam is doing — for the battery."
    bossReport [
        ^boss state printString,
         (abducting = 1 ifTrue: [ ' abducting' ] ifFalse: [
            abducting = 2 ifTrue: [ ' freeing' ] ifFalse: [ '' ] ])
    ]
    bossOn [ ^bossOn ]
    "How many pilots the boss has actually carried off — a LIFETIME count, so a
     test is not fooled by the game resetting under it."
    pilotsTaken [ ^pilotsTaken ]
    abductReport [
        ^'abductee y ', abducteeY printString, ' target ', (boss y + 26) printString,
         ' beamT ', boss beamT printString
    ]

    "Where the saucer is and whether its warble is running — for the battery."
    saucerReport [
        ^saucerDir = 0
            ifTrue: [ 'saucer away' ]
            ifFalse: [ 'saucer at ', saucerX printString,
                       ' warble in ', saucerWah printString ]
    ]

    "Skip to the next wave — the battery's way to walk the level table without
     playing twelve waves out."
    forceNextWave [
        wave := wave + 1.
        self startWave.
        gameState := #playing
    ]

    summary [
        ^gameState printString, ' score ', score printString,
         ' lives ', lives printString, ' wave ', wave printString,
         ' alive ', self aliveCount printString
    ]

    "--- the frame --------------------------------------------------------"

    step [
        frame := frame + 1.
        gameState == #playing ifTrue: [ self stepPlay ].
        gameState == #attract ifTrue: [ self stepAttract ].
        gameState == #cleared ifTrue: [ self stepCleared ].
        gameState == #over ifTrue: [ self stepOver ].
        gameState == #hiscore ifTrue: [ self stepHiscores ].
        self draw.
        pane present
    ]

    stepAttract [
        "The title, with the fleet swaying behind it. Fire starts a game — and
         if nobody does, the title hands over to the hall of fame and the cabinet
         keeps cycling title, table, title, ... for as long as it is left alone.
         That loop is the whole point of an attract mode: the hall of fame is not
         somewhere the machine ENDS up after a game, it is one of the two faces
         the machine shows while it waits for a player."
        self swayFleet.
        fleet do: [ :a | a alive ifTrue: [ a followFormation: swayX ] ].
        (self firePressed) ifTrue: [
            gameState := #playing.
            self startWave.
            (Tune fromAbc: self class tuneTitle) playOnce.
            ^self ].
        stateTimer := stateTimer - 1.
        stateTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [ self showHiscores ]
    ]

    "Show the hall of fame with nothing highlighted — the attract cycle's turn
     at the table, as opposed to enterHiscores, which arrives with a fresh score
     to slot in and a row to flash."
    showHiscores [
        hiNewRow := 0.
        gameState := #hiscore.
        stateTimer := self class hiscoreLength
    ]

    stepCleared [
        stateTimer := stateTimer - 1.
        stateTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [
            wave := wave + 1.
            gameState := #playing.
            self startWave ]
    ]

    "Game over: the survivors break formation and dance. Ported from the
     original's AlienDance — the angle steps once a frame plus each alien's own
     offset around the wheel, and the radius breathes at HALF that rate, so the
     pinwheel opens and closes as it turns. Integer sines throughout (the same
     256-entry table the dive weave uses), so it is exactly reproducible."
    stepOver [
        stateTimer := stateTimer - 1.
        danceT := danceT + 1.
        self dance.
        self stepSparks.
        stateTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [
            score > hiScore ifTrue: [ hiScore := score ].
            self enterHiscores ]
    ]

    "The dance is over: slot the score into the hall (sorted, six rows, named
     YOU — the original's own InsertHiScore), persist the hall through the
     image host if one is listening, and show the table for a few seconds
     before the attract resumes."
    enterHiscores [
        | fresh inserted |
        hiNewRow := 0.
        fresh := OrderedCollection new.
        inserted := false.
        hiTable do: [ :r |
            (inserted not and: [ score > (r at: 2) ]) ifTrue: [
                fresh add: (Array with: 'YOU' with: score).
                inserted := true.
                hiNewRow := fresh size ].
            fresh add: r ].
        inserted ifTrue: [
            [ fresh size > 6 ] whileTrue: [ fresh removeLast ].
            hiTable := fresh.
            Galaxigans saveHall: hiTable.
            "saveHall STORES rather than accepts (see it), so the world is no
             longer hot-reloaded underneath the running frame loop and Current
             survives. Re-register anyway: it costs nothing, and it keeps the
             control plane and the next save pointed at the running game however
             the save was made."
            Galaxigans register: self ].
        gameState := #hiscore.
        stateTimer := self class hiscoreLength
    ]

    stepHiscores [
        stateTimer := stateTimer - 1.
        stateTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [ self newGame ]
    ]

    dance [
        | i |
        i := 0.
        fleet do: [ :a |
            a alive ifTrue: [ | radius angle |
                radius := self class danceR0 +
                    ((Galaxigans sineAt: (danceT // 2) + (i * self class danceRadStep))
                        * self class danceR1 // 256).
                angle := danceT + (i * self class danceAngleStep).
                a moveToX: self class danceCX +
                        ((Galaxigans sineAt: angle + 64) * radius // 256)
                  y: self class danceCY +
                        ((Galaxigans sineAt: angle) * radius // 256).
                i := i + 1 ] ]
    ]

    stepPlay [
        respawn > 0
            ifTrue: [ respawn := respawn - 1 ]
            ifFalse: [ self stepShip ].
        self stepBullets.
        self stepBombs.
        self swayFleet.
        self stepFleet.
        self stepSaucer.
        self stepMines.
        self stepBoss.
        self stepSparks.
        self checkCollisions.
        (fleet anySatisfy: [ :a | a alive ]) ifFalse: [
            gameState := #cleared.
            stateTimer := 120.
            (Tune fromAbc: self class tuneStageClear) playOnce ]
    ]

    "--- the player -------------------------------------------------------"

    stepShip [
        | speed |
        speed := 4.
        (pane keyHeld: GamePane keyLeft) ifTrue: [ shipX := shipX - speed ].
        (pane keyHeld: GamePane keyRight) ifTrue: [ shipX := shipX + speed ].
        shipX := (shipX max: 12) min: self class fieldWidth - 12.
        cooldown > 0 ifTrue: [ cooldown := cooldown - 1 ].
        self firePressed ifTrue: [ self fire ]
    ]

    "Tap to fire: the key must be RELEASED between shots (the original's
     shoot_held / shoot_release_frames). Holding Space does nothing."
    firePressed [
        | down pressed |
        down := pane keyHeld: GamePane keyA.
        pressed := down and: [ fireWasDown not ].
        fireWasDown := down.
        ^pressed
    ]

    fire [
        cooldown > 0 ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        bullets do: [ :b |
            b live ifFalse: [
                b fireFrom: shipX y: self class playerY - 12 dy: -7.
                cooldown := 8.
                Sound shoot play.
                ^self ] ]
    ]

    stepBullets [
        bullets do: [ :b | b stepIn: self class fieldHeight ]
    ]

    "--- the fleet --------------------------------------------------------"

    swayFleet [
        swayX := swayX + swayDir.
        swayX >= 16 ifTrue: [ swayDir := -1 ].
        swayX <= -16 ifTrue: [ swayDir := 1 ]
    ]

    stepFleet [
        diveTimer := diveTimer - 1.
        diveTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [
            diveTimer := self divePeriodNow.
            self launchDiver ].
        bombTimer := bombTimer - 1.
        bombTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [
            bombTimer := self class bombPeriod.
            self dropBomb ].
        fleet do: [ :a |
            a alive ifTrue: [
                a state == #dive
                    ifTrue: [
                        (a diveStep: shipX height: self class fieldHeight)
                            ifTrue: [ a reenterAt: swayX ] ]
                    ifFalse: [
                        a state == #return
                            ifTrue: [ a returnStep: swayX ]
                            ifFalse: [ a followFormation: swayX ] ] ] ]
    ]

    "Pick a live alien still sitting in formation and launch it, with a random
     seed for its flight plan."
    launchDiver [
        | candidates |
        candidates := OrderedCollection new.
        fleet do: [ :a |
            (a alive and: [ a state == #form ]) ifTrue: [ candidates add: a ] ].
        candidates isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        (candidates at: (rng next * candidates size) truncated + 1)
            diveWithSeed: (rng next * 65535) truncated
    ]

    "The lowest diver drops the bomb — a bomb from the back of the formation
     would be a free hit on nobody."
    dropBomb [
        | lowest |
        lowest := nil.
        fleet do: [ :a |
            (a alive and: [ a isDiving ]) ifTrue: [
                (lowest isNil or: [ a y > lowest y ]) ifTrue: [ lowest := a ] ] ].
        lowest isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        bombs do: [ :b |
            b live ifFalse: [
                b fireFrom: lowest x y: lowest y + 10 dy: 4.
                ^self ] ]
    ]

    stepBombs [
        bombs do: [ :b | b stepIn: self class fieldHeight ]
    ]

    "--- the bonus saucer -------------------------------------------------"

    stepSaucer [
        saucerDir = 0
            ifTrue: [
                saucerTimer := saucerTimer - 1.
                saucerTimer <= 0 ifTrue: [
                    saucerTimer := self class saucerPeriod.
                    saucerDir := (rng next < 0.5) ifTrue: [ 1 ] ifFalse: [ -1 ].
                    saucerWah := 0.               "start the warble on arrival"
                    (Tune fromAbc: self class tuneSaucer) playOnce.
                    saucerX := saucerDir > 0
                        ifTrue: [ -30 ]
                        ifFalse: [ self class fieldWidth + 30 ] ] ]
            ifFalse: [
                saucerX := saucerX + (saucerDir * 2).
                self warble.
                self saucerDrop.
                (saucerX < -40 or: [ saucerX > (self class fieldWidth + 40) ])
                    ifTrue: [ saucerDir := 0. saucer hide ] ]
    ]

    "The saucer lobs something from its belly every 28 frames while it is over
     the field — and about one drop in eight is a MINE rather than a bomb, which
     is the original's own ratio (Rng & 7). The rare one is the interesting one:
     a bomb is gone in two seconds, a mine hangs there."
    saucerDrop [
        (saucerX < 0 or: [ saucerX > (self class fieldWidth - 16) ]) ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        saucerBombT := saucerBombT - 1.
        saucerBombT > 0 ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        saucerBombT := self class saucerBombGap.
        saucerDrops := saucerDrops + 1.
        (rng next * 8) truncated = 0
            ifTrue: [
                mines do: [ :m |
                    m live ifFalse: [
                        m dropAt: saucerX y: self class saucerY + 12.
                        mineDrops := mineDrops + 1.
                        ^self ] ] ]
            ifFalse: [
                bombs do: [ :b |
                    b live ifFalse: [
                        b fireFrom: saucerX y: self class saucerY + 12 dy: 4.
                        ^self ] ] ]
    ]

    stepMines [
        mines do: [ :m | m stepIn: self class fieldHeight ]
    ]

    "--- the capture boss ---------------------------------------------------"

    stepBoss [
        | event |
        "A freed pilot falls home from wherever the beam had got it to — that
         runs in ANY boss state, including after the boss is gone."
        abducting = 2 ifTrue: [
            abducteeY := abducteeY + 5.
            abducteeY >= self class pilotRowY ifTrue: [ abducting := 0 ] ].

        event := boss stepWithLives: lives enabled: bossOn.
        event == #warn ifTrue: [ Sound hurt play ].
        event == #charged ifTrue: [ Sound bossHum play ].
        event == #done ifTrue: [ self releasePilot ].
        event == #grab ifTrue: [ self dragPilot ].
        boss isBeaming ifTrue: [ self cascadeBeam ]
    ]

    "The abduction: a pilot leaves the row and rises up the beam. It reaching
     the boss costs a life — and if that was the last one, the aliens have won
     and the dance begins."
    dragPilot [
        abducting = 0 ifTrue: [
            lives <= 1 ifTrue: [ ^self ].       "never take the last pilot"
            abducting := 1.
            abducteeX := boss beamX - 6.
            abducteeY := self class pilotRowY.
            ^self ].
        abducting = 1 ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        abducteeY := abducteeY - 3.
        abducteeY > (boss y + 26) ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        "It made it to the boss."
        lives := lives - 1.
        pilotsTaken := pilotsTaken + 1.
        abducting := 0.
        Sound hurt play.
        self burstAt: boss beamX y: boss y + 26 colour: 22.
        lives <= 0
            ifTrue: [ self beginDance. boss vanish ]
            ifFalse: [ boss retreat ]
    ]

    "The beam times out with nobody taken: whatever is halfway up falls home."
    releasePilot [
        abducting = 1 ifTrue: [ abducting := 2 ]
    ]

    "Shooting the boss frees any pilot in the beam (it drops home, saved) and
     pays 500 — the best thing on the screen, and the reason to take the risk
     of standing under a tractor beam."
    checkBossHit [
        bullets do: [ :b |
            (b live and: [ boss hits: b x y: b y ]) ifTrue: [
                b kill.
                score := score + self class bossScore.
                self burstAt: boss x + 16 y: boss y + 16 colour: 23.
                Sound explode play.
                self releasePilot.
                boss retreat.
                ^self ] ]
    ]

    "The beam's colour FLOWS without redrawing a pixel: the cone is drawn once
     in palette index 1, and index 1 means something different on every
     scanline. Stepping the ramp by (y + phase) each frame sends the bands
     downward — the copper-bar trick, and the original's own (BeamCascade)."
    cascadeBeam [
        | top bot ramp |
        top := boss beamTop.
        bot := boss beamBottom: self class fieldHeight.
        ramp := self class beamRamp.
        beamPhase := beamPhase + 1.
        top to: bot do: [ :y |
            (y >= 0 and: [ y < self class fieldHeight ]) ifTrue: [ | k |
                k := ((y - top + beamPhase) // 2) \\ 8.
                pane linePaletteAt: y index: 1
                     r: (ramp at: k * 3 + 1)
                     g: (ramp at: k * 3 + 2)
                     b: (ramp at: k * 3 + 3) ] ]
    ]

    "The cyan energy ramp, pulsing dim -> white -> dim so it reads as flow."
    Galaxigans class >> beamRamp [
        ^#(16 48 64   28 96 120   48 152 184   88 200 232
           176 244 255   88 200 232   48 152 184   28 96 120)
    ]

    "The saucer's wah-wah: two sines five Hz apart, beating against each other.
     One note runs 0.9s and the crossing takes six, so it is re-triggered on a
     loop while the saucer is on screen — the original does exactly this
     (PlaySaucerWah), and it is why the warble seems to go on forever and then
     simply stops when the saucer leaves."
    warble [
        saucerWah > 0
            ifTrue: [ saucerWah := saucerWah - 1 ]
            ifFalse: [ saucerWah := 50. Sound saucer play ]
    ]

    "--- collisions -------------------------------------------------------"

    checkCollisions [
        bullets do: [ :b |
            b live ifTrue: [
                (saucerDir ~= 0 and: [ b hits: saucerX y: self class saucerY + 4
                                        halfWidth: 12 halfHeight: 8 ])
                    ifTrue: [
                        b kill.
                        score := score + 200.
                        self burstAt: saucerX y: self class saucerY + 4 colour: 22.
                        Sound coin play.
                        saucerDir := 0.
                        saucer moveTo: -80 y: -80 ].
                b live ifTrue: [
                    fleet do: [ :a |
                        (b live and: [ a hits: b x y: b y halfWidth: 4 ]) ifTrue: [
                            b kill.
                            score := score + a points.
                            self burstAt: a x y: a y colour: 23.
                            Sound explode play.
                            a kill.
                            a sprite hide ] ] ] ] ].

        self checkBossHit.

        "Shooting a mine is the treat: 150, the best points on the screen."
        bullets do: [ :b |
            b live ifTrue: [
                mines do: [ :m |
                    (b live and: [ m hits: b x y: b y halfWidth: 4 halfHeight: 4 ])
                        ifTrue: [
                            b kill.
                            m kill.
                            m sprite hide.
                            score := score + self class mineScore.
                            self burstAt: m x y: m y colour: 22.
                            Sound bang play ] ] ] ].

        respawn > 0 ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        "And touching one is the threat."
        mines do: [ :m |
            (m hits: shipX y: self class playerY halfWidth: 6 halfHeight: 6)
                ifTrue: [ m kill. m sprite hide. self loseLife ] ].
        bombs do: [ :b |
            (b hits: shipX y: self class playerY halfWidth: 8 halfHeight: 10)
                ifTrue: [ b kill. self loseLife ] ].
        fleet do: [ :a |
            (a isDiving and: [ a hits: shipX y: self class playerY halfWidth: 6 ])
                ifTrue: [
                    self burstAt: a x y: a y colour: 23.
                    a kill.
                    a sprite hide.
                    self loseLife ] ]
    ]

    loseLife [
        self burstAt: shipX y: self class playerY colour: 22.
        Sound hurt play.
        lives := lives - 1.
        respawn := 90.
        shipX := self class fieldWidth // 2.
        lives <= 0 ifTrue: [ self beginDance ]
    ]

    "--- explosions -------------------------------------------------------"

    burstAt: bx y: by colour: c [
        | n |
        n := 14.
        1 to: n do: [ :i | | ang |
            ang := (i * 256 // n).
            sparks add: (GxSpark
                at: bx y: by
                vx: (Galaxigans sineAt: ang) * 5 // 256
                vy: (Galaxigans sineAt: ang + 64) * 5 // 256 - 2
                colour: c) ].
        sparks size > 240 ifTrue: [ sparks removeFirst ]
    ]

    stepSparks [
        | keep |
        keep := OrderedCollection new.
        sparks do: [ :s | s step. s live ifTrue: [ keep add: s ] ].
        sparks := keep
    ]

    "--- drawing ----------------------------------------------------------"

    draw [
        "Index 0 is transparent, so clearing to it leaves the SHADER visible
         underneath — the indexed layer carries only the game's own pixels."
        pane cls: 0.
        sparks do: [ :s |
            pane fill: s x y: s y width: 2 height: 2 color: s colour ].
        bullets do: [ :b |
            b live ifTrue: [
                pane fill: b x - 1 y: b y width: 3 height: 8 color: 20 ] ].
        bombs do: [ :b |
            b live ifTrue: [
                pane fill: b x - 2 y: b y width: 4 height: 6 color: 21 ] ].
        self drawBeam.
        self placeSprites.
        self drawHud
    ]

    "The tractor beam: a cone widening from the boss's mouth to the floor,
     drawn ONCE per frame in palette index 1 — whose colour the cascade has
     already made different on every scanline. Half-width goes 4 -> 20 down its
     length, which is the original's own taper."
    drawBeam [
        | top bot span |
        boss isBeaming ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        top := boss beamTop.
        bot := boss beamBottom: self class fieldHeight.
        span := (bot - top) max: 1.
        top to: bot do: [ :y |
            | hw |
            hw := 4 + ((y - top) * 16 // span).
            pane fill: boss beamX - hw y: y width: hw * 2 height: 1 color: 1 ]
    ]

    placeSprites [
        "Sprites are placed by their top-left, so everything is drawn from its
         centre minus half its art. The fleet flaps: every eighth frame the
         whole formation switches to its species' second frame. The high-score
         scene stands alone: everything hides while the table is up."
        gameState == #hiscore ifTrue: [
            fleet do: [ :a | a sprite hide ].
            mines do: [ :m | m sprite hide ].
            boss sprite hide.
            pilots do: [ :spr | spr hide ].
            saucer hide.
            shipSprite hide.
            ^self ].
        flap := (frame // 8) \\ 2.
        fleet do: [ :a |
            a alive
                ifTrue: [ a sprite moveTo: a x - 8 y: a y - 8
                                   frame: (a frameFor: flap) ]
                ifFalse: [ a sprite hide ] ].
        mines do: [ :m |
            m live
                ifTrue: [ m sprite moveTo: m x - 8 y: m y - 8 frame: m frame ]
                ifFalse: [ m sprite hide ] ].
        boss isIdle
            ifTrue: [ boss sprite hide ]
            ifFalse: [ boss sprite moveTo: boss x y: boss y frame: boss frame ].
        self placePilots.
        saucerDir = 0
            ifTrue: [ saucer hide ]
            ifFalse: [ saucer moveTo: saucerX - 10 y: self class saucerY ].
        (gameState == #playing and: [ respawn = 0 ])
            ifTrue: [ shipSprite moveTo: shipX - 8 y: self class playerY - 7 ]
            ifFalse: [
                "Blink through the respawn pause instead of vanishing."
                (respawn > 0 and: [ (respawn // 4) \\ 2 = 0 ])
                    ifTrue: [ shipSprite moveTo: shipX - 8 y: self class playerY - 7 ]
                    ifFalse: [ shipSprite hide ] ]
    ]

    "The pilots standing along the bottom: one per life. A pilot in the beam has
     LEFT the row — it is drawn wherever the beam has dragged it to, and it is
     still yours until it reaches the boss."
    placePilots [
        | inRow |
        inRow := abducting > 0 ifTrue: [ lives - 1 ] ifFalse: [ lives ].
        1 to: pilots size do: [ :i |
            i <= inRow
                ifTrue: [ (pilots at: i)
                            moveTo: self class pilotX0 + ((i - 1) * self class pilotGap)
                            y: self class pilotRowY ]
                ifFalse: [ (pilots at: i) hide ] ].
        abducting > 0 ifTrue: [
            (pilots at: pilots size) moveTo: abducteeX y: abducteeY ]
    ]

    "Six digits, zero-padded — the arcade's own score format (HiFmt)."
    score6: n [
        | t |
        t := n printString.
        [ t size < 6 ] whileTrue: [ t := '0', t ].
        ^t
    ]

    drawHiscores [
        | y r |
        pane textClear.
        pane text: 'H I G H   S C O R E S'
             x: 130 y: 46 r: 255 g: 210 b: 60 scale: 3.
        y := 110.
        1 to: hiTable size do: [ :i |
            r := hiTable at: i.
            "The row you just took blinks gold; the rest sit quiet."
            (i = hiNewRow and: [ (frame // 8) \\ 2 = 0 ])
                ifTrue: [
                    pane text: i printString, '  ', (r at: 1), '  ', (self score6: (r at: 2))
                         x: 190 y: y r: 255 g: 220 b: 90 scale: 2 ]
                ifFalse: [
                    pane text: i printString, '  ', (r at: 1), '  ', (self score6: (r at: 2))
                         x: 190 y: y
                         r: (i = hiNewRow ifTrue: [ 255 ] ifFalse: [ 150 ])
                         g: (i = hiNewRow ifTrue: [ 220 ] ifFalse: [ 200 ])
                         b: (i = hiNewRow ifTrue: [ 90 ] ifFalse: [ 255 ])
                         scale: 2 ].
            y := y + 26 ].
        hiNewRow > 0 ifTrue: [
            pane text: 'A PLACE IN THE HALL'
                 x: 208 y: 300 r: 120 g: 255 b: 140 scale: 2 ]
    ]

    drawHud [
        gameState == #hiscore ifTrue: [ ^self drawHiscores ].
        pane textClear.
        pane text: 'SCORE ', score printString
             x: 10 y: 8 r: 255 g: 255 b: 255 scale: 2.
        pane text: 'HI ', (hiScore max: score) printString
             x: 250 y: 8 r: 255 g: 220 b: 90 scale: 2.
        pane text: 'WAVE ', wave printString
             x: 440 y: 8 r: 140 g: 220 b: 255 scale: 2.
        pane text: (self class sceneNames at: scene + 1)
             x: 440 y: 336 r: 150 g: 150 b: 190 scale: 2.
        pane text: 'SHIPS ', lives printString
             x: 10 y: 336 r: 120 g: 200 b: 255 scale: 2.
        gameState == #attract ifTrue: [
            pane text: 'GALAXIGANS' x: 176 y: 140 r: 255 g: 210 b: 60 scale: 5.
            pane text: 'SPACE TO START   ARROWS TO STEER'
                 x: 152 y: 200 r: 220 g: 220 b: 255 scale: 2 ].
        gameState == #cleared ifTrue: [
            pane text: 'WAVE CLEARED' x: 200 y: 150 r: 120 g: 255 b: 140 scale: 4.
            pane text: 'NEXT: ', (self class sceneNames
                                     at: ((self class levels
                                             at: wave \\ self class levels size + 1)
                                          at: 1) + 1)
                 x: 200 y: 200 r: 220 g: 220 b: 255 scale: 2 ].
        gameState == #over ifTrue: [
            pane text: 'GAME OVER' x: 220 y: 160 r: 255 g: 90 b: 90 scale: 4.
            pane text: 'SCORE ', score printString
                 x: 236 y: 210 r: 255 g: 220 b: 120 scale: 2 ]
    ]


    "--- the creature library, the level table, and the cosmos --------------"

    "Ten species, built once. Their art and palettes are the assembler's own."
    Galaxigans class >> species [
        "Built one at a time: Array class>>with: stops at five arguments, and
         ten species is exactly the kind of place that runs out."
        Species isNil ifTrue: [
            Species := Array new: 10.
            Species at: 1  put: self gruntSpecies.
            Species at: 2  put: self mothSpecies.
            Species at: 3  put: self beetleSpecies.
            Species at: 4  put: self scorpionSpecies.
            Species at: 5  put: self mantisSpecies.
            Species at: 6  put: self hornetSpecies.
            Species at: 7  put: self jellyfishSpecies.
            Species at: 8  put: self spiderSpecies.
            Species at: 9  put: self stingraySpecies.
            Species at: 10 put: self squidSpecies ].
        ^Species
    ]

    "Formation themes: the species for grid rows 1..5, top row first (and the
     top row is the toughest). The original ships four themes and rotates them
     through the level table — classic, then the newer species, then a mix."
    Galaxigans class >> themes [
        ^#(
            #(6 2 1 1 3)      "classic:   hornet moth grunt grunt beetle"
            #(6 9 2 3 1)      "+ray:      hornet stingray moth beetle grunt"
            #(10 7 9 8 5)     "new-heavy: squid jellyfish stingray spider mantis"
            #(7 6 9 4 2)      "full mix:  jellyfish hornet stingray scorpion moth"
        )
    ]

    "The level table, ported row for row: {cosmos scene, formation theme}. The
     scene is which of the twelve backdrops the layer-0 shader draws; levels
     past the last row wrap it, and the dive cadence keeps tightening."
    Galaxigans class >> levels [
        "{cosmos scene, formation theme, capture boss?} — the original's own
         table, boss column and all: it turns up every third level."
        ^#(
            #(0 1 0)  #(1 2 0)  #(2 3 1)   #(3 4 0)
            #(4 1 0)  #(5 2 1)  #(6 3 0)   #(7 4 0)
            #(8 1 1)  #(9 2 0)  #(10 3 0)  #(11 4 1)
        )
    ]

    Galaxigans class >> sceneNames [
        ^#('NEBULA' 'GALAXY' 'BLACK HOLE' 'ALIEN WORLD' 'MOON' 'SUPERNOVA'
           'WORMHOLE' 'GAS GIANT' 'AURORA' 'PULSAR' 'PLASMA' 'BINARY STARS')
    ]

    "The twelve cosmos backdrops, as one Metal fragment shader with the scene in
     shader parameter 0. Translated from the original's HLSL (its starfield
     module compiles the same twelve scenes for D3D) — same maths, same
     constants, Metal spelling: frac->fract, lerp->mix, and the aspect the
     original hardcodes as 1.7778 taken from the uniform instead."
    Galaxigans class >> cosmosShader [
        ^'float h21(float2 p) { return fract(sin(dot(p, float2(127.1, 311.7))) * 43758.5453); }

float3 scNebula(float2 uv, float t) {
    float px = uv.x * 640.0, py = uv.y * 360.0;
    float n = sin(px*0.011 + t*0.30) + sin(py*0.014 - t*0.20)
            + sin((px+py)*0.007 + t*0.15) + sin((px-py)*0.009 - t*0.10);
    float neb = (n + 4.0) * 0.125;
    float3 col = float3(0.015 + neb*0.05, 0.010 + neb*0.03, 0.055 + neb*0.20);
    for (int L = 0; L < 3; L++) {
        float sp = 16.0 + float(L)*30.0, cell = 13.0 + float(L)*6.0;
        float2 cp = float2(px, py - t*sp) / cell;
        float2 gi = floor(cp);
        float h = h21(gi);
        if (h > 0.90) {
            float2 sub = fract(cp) - 0.5;
            float d = dot(sub, sub);
            float tw = 0.55 + 0.45*sin(t*3.0 + h*50.0);
            col += saturate(1.0 - d*55.0) * tw * (0.45 + 0.5*float(L));
        }
    }
    return col;
}

float3 scGalaxy(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c); float a = atan2(c.y, c.x);
    float spiral = sin(2.0*(a + t*0.15) + 6.5*log(r + 0.06));
    float arm = smoothstep(0.0, 0.7, spiral) * exp(-r*2.6);
    float core = exp(-r*r*38.0);
    float3 col = float3(0.04, 0.02, 0.09);
    col += arm * float3(0.45, 0.40, 0.85) * 0.7;
    col += core * float3(1.0, 0.9, 0.7);
    col += arm * 0.35 * float3(0.8, 0.5, 0.95) * (0.5 + 0.5*sin(r*60.0 - t));
    float2 sg = c*70.0; float2 sgi = floor(sg); float sh = h21(sgi);
    float2 ssb = fract(sg) - 0.5; float sd = dot(ssb, ssb);
    col += (sh > 0.93 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * saturate(1.0 - sd*55.0) * 0.6 * saturate(1.4 - r*2.0);
    return col;
}

float3 scBlack(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c); float a = atan2(c.y, c.x);
    float horizon = smoothstep(0.12, 0.105, r);
    float rr = (r - 0.19)*8.5; float ring = exp(-rr*rr);
    float swirl = 0.55 + 0.45*sin(a*3.0 - t*2.2 + 22.0*r);
    float3 disk = ring * swirl * float3(1.0, 0.55, 0.18);
    float2 lp = c * (1.0 + 0.04/(r*r + 0.02));
    float2 sg = lp*72.0; float2 sgi = floor(sg); float sh = h21(sgi);
    float2 ssb = fract(sg) - 0.5; float sd = dot(ssb, ssb);
    float stars = (sh > 0.95 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * saturate(1.0 - sd*45.0) * smoothstep(0.11, 0.15, r);
    float3 col = disk + stars*0.7 + float3(0.02, 0.01, 0.03);
    col *= (1.0 - horizon);
    return col;
}

float3 scAlien(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float3 sky = mix(float3(0.02,0.05,0.08), float3(0.10,0.03,0.13), uv.y);
    float2 pc = uv - float2(0.5, 1.18); pc.x *= aspect;
    float pr = length(pc); float planet = smoothstep(0.63, 0.62, pr);
    float bands = 0.5 + 0.5*sin(pc.y*34.0 + sin(pc.x*7.0 + t*0.2)*2.2);
    float3 psurf = mix(float3(0.20,0.45,0.18), float3(0.55,0.70,0.30), bands);
    float z = sqrt(saturate(0.40 - pr*pr));
    float lit = saturate(dot(normalize(float3(pc.x, pc.y, z*1.5)),
                             normalize(float3(-0.5, -0.6, 0.6))));
    psurf *= 0.25 + 0.95*lit;
    float3 col = mix(sky, psurf, planet);
    float st = h21(floor(uv * float2(220.0, 130.0)));
    col += (st > 0.985 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * (1.0 - planet) * 0.8;
    float2 mc = uv - float2(0.80, 0.22); mc.x *= aspect; float mr = length(mc);
    float moon = smoothstep(0.05, 0.045, mr);
    float ml = saturate(dot(normalize(float3(mc.x, mc.y, 0.05)),
                            normalize(float3(-0.4, -0.5, 0.7))));
    col = mix(col, float3(0.55,0.52,0.48) * (0.4 + 0.7*ml), moon);
    return col;
}

float craterH(float2 uv) {
    float h = 0.0;
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
        float sc = 5.0 * pow(1.8, float(k));
        float2 p = uv*sc; float2 gi = floor(p); float2 gf = fract(p) - 0.5;
        float2 off = float2(h21(gi) - 0.5, h21(gi + 3.3) - 0.5) * 0.5;
        float d = length(gf - off); float rad = 0.16 + 0.16*h21(gi + 7.7);
        float rim = smoothstep(rad + 0.05, rad, d) * smoothstep(rad - 0.06, rad, d);
        float bowl = smoothstep(rad, 0.0, d);
        h += (rim*0.6 - bowl*0.35) / (float(k) + 1.0);
    }
    return h;
}

float3 scMoon(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 uvp = uv + float2(t*0.008, 0.0); uvp.x *= aspect;
    float cr = craterH(uvp);
    float fine = h21(floor(uv * float2(320.0, 180.0))) * 0.05;
    float3 col = float3(0.22,0.22,0.24) + cr*float3(0.55,0.54,0.58) + fine;
    return saturate(col);
}

float3 scNova(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c); float a = atan2(c.y, c.x);
    float ph = fract(t*0.12);
    float er = (r - ph*0.75)*7.0; float ring = exp(-er*er);
    float core = exp(-r*r*26.0) * (1.3 - ph);
    float rays = 0.6 + 0.4*sin(a*20.0 + t);
    float3 col = float3(0.05, 0.02, 0.05);
    col += core * float3(1.0, 0.92, 0.7);
    col += ring * float3(1.0, 0.55, 0.25) * rays;
    float st = h21(floor(c*55.0));
    col += (st > 0.95 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * 0.35 * saturate(1.3 - r);
    return col;
}

float3 scWormhole(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c) + 0.05; float a = atan2(c.y, c.x);
    float depth = 0.32/r + t*0.6;
    float ring = 0.5 + 0.5*sin(depth*9.0);
    float twist = 0.5 + 0.5*sin(a*6.0 + depth*2.5);
    float3 col = mix(float3(0.02,0.04,0.10), float3(0.20,0.55,0.95), ring*twist);
    col *= saturate(r*2.6);
    col += exp(-r*r*55.0) * float3(0.7, 0.85, 1.0);
    return col;
}

float3 scGasGiant(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - float2(0.5, 0.44); c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c); float planet = smoothstep(0.32, 0.31, r);
    float lat = c.y/0.33;
    float bands = 0.5 + 0.5*sin(lat*15.0 + sin(lat*4.0 + t*0.1)*1.4);
    float3 surf = mix(float3(0.55,0.42,0.24), float3(0.85,0.72,0.46), bands);
    float2 sp = c - float2(0.11, -0.04);
    float spot = smoothstep(0.06, 0.0, length(sp * float2(1.0, 1.7)));
    surf = mix(surf, float3(0.82,0.32,0.20), spot*0.7);
    float z = sqrt(saturate(0.105 - r*r));
    float lit = saturate(dot(normalize(float3(c.x, c.y, z*3.0)),
                             normalize(float3(-0.5, -0.3, 0.8))));
    surf *= 0.30 + 0.9*lit;
    float2 rc = c * float2(1.0, 3.4); float rr = length(rc);
    float ring = smoothstep(0.40, 0.43, rr) * smoothstep(0.60, 0.57, rr)
               * (0.55 + 0.45*sin(rr*90.0));
    float3 col = float3(0.02, 0.02, 0.05);
    float st = h21(floor(uv * float2(220.0, 130.0)));
    col += (st > 0.985 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * 0.7;
    col = mix(col, float3(0.75,0.68,0.52), ring * (1.0 - planet));
    col = mix(col, surf, planet);
    return col;
}

float3 scAurora(float2 uv, float t) {
    float3 col = float3(0.01, 0.02, 0.05);
    float st = h21(floor(uv * float2(200.0, 120.0)));
    col += (st > 0.98 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * 0.6 * smoothstep(0.55, 0.0, uv.y);
    float fil = 0.62 + 0.38*sin(uv.x*140.0 + sin(uv.y*8.0)*2.0 + t*1.5);
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        float fi = float(i);
        float cx = 0.18 + fi*0.22 + 0.13*sin(uv.y*3.0 + t*0.4 + fi*1.7);
        float fx = (uv.x - cx)*11.0; float band = exp(-fx*fx);
        float hh = smoothstep(0.04, 0.42, uv.y) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.50, 0.96, uv.y));
        float3 ac = mix(float3(0.1,0.95,0.45), float3(0.45,0.2,0.9), fract(fi*0.37));
        col += band * hh * fil * ac * 0.75;
    }
    return col;
}

float3 scPulsar(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float r = length(c); float a = atan2(c.y, c.x);
    float core = exp(-r*r*70.0);
    float beam = pow(abs(cos(a - t*1.5)), 40.0) + pow(abs(cos(a - t*1.5 + 3.14159)), 40.0);
    beam *= exp(-r*1.6);
    float3 col = float3(0.02, 0.03, 0.06);
    col += core * float3(0.85, 0.92, 1.0);
    col += beam * float3(0.45, 0.65, 1.0);
    float st = h21(floor(c*60.0));
    col += (st > 0.97 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * 0.45;
    return col;
}

float3 scPlasma(float2 uv, float t) {
    float px = uv.x*6.0, py = uv.y*4.0;
    float v = sin(px + t) + sin(py*1.3 - t*0.7) + sin((px+py)*0.8 + t*0.5)
            + sin(length(float2(px, py) - 3.0)*2.2 - t);
    float3 col = 0.5 + 0.5*cos(float3(v, v + 2.1, v + 4.2));
    col *= float3(0.42, 0.30, 0.52);
    return col;
}

float3 scBinary(float2 uv, float t, float aspect) {
    float2 c = uv - 0.5; c.x *= aspect;
    float2 s1 = float2(cos(t*0.4), sin(t*0.4)) * 0.16;
    float2 s2 = -s1;
    float d1 = length(c - s1), d2 = length(c - s2);
    float3 col = float3(0.02, 0.02, 0.05);
    col += exp(-d1*d1*150.0)*float3(1.0,0.8,0.5) + exp(-d1*9.0)*float3(0.35,0.25,0.12);
    col += exp(-d2*d2*150.0)*float3(0.6,0.8,1.0) + exp(-d2*9.0)*float3(0.16,0.26,0.4);
    float st = h21(floor(c*52.0));
    col += (st > 0.97 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * 0.4;
    return col;
}

fragment float4 fmain(VOut in [[stage_in]], constant Uniforms& u [[buffer(0)]]) {
    float t = u.time;
    int sc = int(u.p[0] + 0.5);
    float2 uv = in.uv;
    float a = u.aspect;
    float3 col;
    if (sc == 1) col = scGalaxy(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 2) col = scBlack(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 3) col = scAlien(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 4) col = scMoon(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 5) col = scNova(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 6) col = scWormhole(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 7) col = scGasGiant(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 8) col = scAurora(uv, t);
    else if (sc == 9) col = scPulsar(uv, t, a);
    else if (sc == 10) col = scPlasma(uv, t);
    else if (sc == 11) col = scBinary(uv, t, a);
    else col = scNebula(uv, t);
    return float4(col, 1.0);
}'
    ]

