    "--- the original's music cues (galaxigans_music.was) -------------------"
    "Transcribed note for note from the assembler's inline ABC, which its own
     header traces back to the FreeBASIC original's MUSIC slots. One change,
     and it is a dialect difference rather than a liberty: the assembler writes
     `%%MIDI program <voice> <gm#>`, and this pane's ABC reader takes the GM
     number directly — so `program 1 80` becomes `program 80`, and the square
     lead is the square lead."

    "Slot 10, 'Alien Victory' — the square-lead triumph the aliens dance to when
     they have taken your last ship. GM 80, C minor, and it is THEIR tune: the
     player never hears it in victory."
    Galaxigans class >> tuneAlienVictory [
        ^'X:1
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=210
%%MIDI program 80
K:Cm
V:1
G,4 _B,4 | c4 _e4 | _e2d2c2_B2 | G,8 | G,2G,2_A,2_B,2 | c2_e2g2_e2 | c4_B4 | G,8 | _E2F2G2_A2 | _B2c2_e2g2 | f/e/d/c/_B/A/_A/G/ | _E8 |'
    ]

    "Slot 14, 'Stage Alert' — the ominous choir build on the title screen."
    Galaxigans class >> tuneTitle [
        ^'X:1
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=84
%%MIDI program 52
K:Am
V:1
z4 A,2 E2 | A2 c2 e2 d2 | c4 B4 | A8 |'
    ]

    "Slot 13, 'You Win!' — the glockenspiel fanfare for a cleared wave."
    Galaxigans class >> tuneStageClear [
        ^'X:1
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=234
%%MIDI program 9
K:C
V:1
ceg c'' e''c''ba | gecG c2 z2 | fac''f'' e''d''c''b | c''4 |'
    ]

    "Slot 12, 'Saucer Wooh' — the pad swell that announces the bonus saucer,
     under the warble rather than instead of it (the original plays both)."
    Galaxigans class >> tuneSaucer [
        ^'X:1
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=160
%%MIDI program 91
K:C
V:1
G z G z | GABc cBAG |'
    ]

